      "description": "Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions - Missouri Valley University Skip to content Missouri Valley University Menu About About Mission, Vision, Values, and Goals God, Family, Country Our History Consumer Information Offices Leadership Careers at MVC Morris Gallery of Contemporary Art Faces of Jesus Exhibit Campus & Directions Meet Our Students & Alumni Admissions & Financial Aid Admissions & Financial Aid How to Apply Tuition & Financial Aid Scholarships Visit Missouri Valley International Students New Student Orientation Meet Our Admissions Team Payments/Policies 1098-T Information Student Employment Program Parent Resources Academics Academics Programs of Study Academic Schools Course Offerings Learning Beyond the Classroom New Student Orientation Honors College Graduate Studies MVU Online Dual Credit for High School Students Murrell Library and Academic Support Center Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Faculty Teaching Award Recipients Graduation Information Institutional Review Board Certificate Programs Student Engagement Student Engagement Activities & Events Clubs & Organizations Recreation & Fitness New Student Orientation Student Handbook Housing & Dining Health & Wellness Getting Out & About Campus Chaplain Student Employment Safety & Security Accessibility & Disability Services Student Success Center Title IX News & Events News & Events News Events Publications Social Media Alumni Alumni Homecoming Stay Connected Outstanding Alumni Alumni Recognition Center and Museum Athletic Hall of Fame Nomination Alumni Events Alumni Advisory Board Legacy Scholarship Transcript Request Viking Views Magazine Giving Viking Tailgate Zone Viking Apparel Store Athletics Search Search Search for: MyMoval Faculty & Staff Directory Pay Enrollment Fee Give to MVU Section Navigation Employment Opportunities Director of Athletics Head STUNT Coach Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions Head Cheer Coach Missouri Valley University | About | Employment Opportunities | Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions Adjunct and Graduate Assistant Positions Adjunct Instructor of Psychology Adjunct Instructor of Psychology Institution: Missouri Valley College Department: School of Education and Social Science Delivery Mode: On-Campus The School of Education and Social Science invites applications for on-campus Adjunct Instructor of Psychology to qualified individuals. Collegiality, professionalism, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence and the college mission are required. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Teach assigned course(s) as specified in the course schedule and contract. Guide students to succeed through personal instruction and intellectual inquiry. Prepare and distribute to students a complete and comprehensive syllabus as per institutional guidelines for every course taught. Undertake and monitor initiatives to improve student learning. Respond to student work, communications, and requests in a timely manner. Maintain a positive, productive, and respectful classroom environment. Communicate, collaborate, and coordinate work with colleagues in a timely manner. Complete assigned or accepted responsibilities, including routine administrative tasks, with accuracy and attention to detail by established deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, requirements, and procedures. Representative, but not all inclusive, of the essential job functions/responsibilities required for this position. Qualifications Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Psychology from an accredited institution required. Terminal degree in Psychology or a related field from an accredited institution preferred. Previous teaching experience in a college or university setting is preferred. In evaluating candidates for this position, a combination of education, training, and experience which provides the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position may be considered. Physical Demands Stamina to teach classes as required. Ability to stand or sit for extended time periods. Regular attendance is a necessary and essential function. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to engage in effective interactions with students, employees, alumni, and other stakeholders, including individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Ability to think critically and solve problems independently. Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills. Ability to work effectively and independently in a remote teaching environment with minimal supervision. Ability to provide an unwavering example of professionalism. Working knowledge of Google Workspace preferred. Working knowledge of Canvas or an equivalent learning management system required. Ability to successfully complete the MVC Online Masterclass (applies to online instructors only). Representative, but not all-inclusive, of the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for this position. Work Environment Home Office (Online Instructors) General classroom and office settings (On-campus Instructors) Required Technology (Online Instructors Only) Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Dependable, high-speed Internet access. The required browser is Chrome. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Compensation varies by course based on student enrollment and program type. Application Instructions Please send cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to Dean Zachary Templeton at templetonz@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, Adjunct Instructor of Communications Adjunct Instructor of Communication Institution: Missouri Valley College Department: School of Arts and Humanities Delivery Mode: On-Campus, Face-to-Face The School of Arts and Humanities invites applications from qualified individuals for on-campus, face-to-face Adjunct Instructor of Communication Studies opportunities. Collegiality, professionalism, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence and the college mission are required. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Teach assigned course(s) such as Public Speaking, Interpersonal Communication, and Argumentation and Debate as specified in the course schedule and contract. Guide students to succeed through personal instruction and intellectual inquiry. Prepare and distribute to students a complete and comprehensive syllabus as per institutional guidelines for every course taught. Undertake and monitor initiatives to improve student learning. Respond to student work, communications, and requests in a timely manner. Maintain a positive, productive, and respectful classroom environment. Communicate, collaborate, and coordinate work with colleagues in a timely manner. Complete assigned or accepted responsibilities, including routine administrative tasks, with accuracy and attention to detail by established deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, requirements, and procedures. Representative, but not all inclusive, of the essential job functions/responsibilities required for this position. Qualifications Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Communication Studies from an accredited institution required. Terminal degree in Communication Studies or a related field from an accredited institution preferred. Previous teaching experience in a college or university setting is preferred. In evaluating candidates for this position, a combination of education, training, and experience which provides the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position may be considered. Physical Demands Stamina to teach classes as required. Ability to stand or sit for extended time periods. Regular attendance is a necessary and essential function. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to engage in effective interactions with students, employees, alumni, and other stakeholders, including individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Ability to think critically and solve problems independently. Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills. Ability to work effectively and independently with minimal supervision. Ability to provide an unwavering example of professionalism. Working knowledge of Google Workspace preferred. Working knowledge of Canvas or an equivalent learning management system required. Representative, but not all-inclusive, of the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for this position. Work Environment General classroom and office settings (on-campus Instructors) Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Compensation varies by course based on student enrollment and program type. Application Instructions Please send cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to Kelley McKay Fuemmeler at mckayk@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall Graduate Assistant, School of Business and Technology Graduate Assistant for the School of Business and Technology will perform the role of an Office Manager and support the Dean and the daily operations of the School of Business and Technology. Responsibilities: Provide administrative support to the Dean in the day-to-day operations of the School of Business and Technology Assist with research, data management, and reporting Liaise with other departments as needed. Assist with school-sponsored events (MIE, guest speakers, workshops, networking, etc.) Assist faculty and students in utilizing technology tools, software, and platforms relevant to the School of Business and Technology. Maintain office efficiency by planning and implementing office systems, layouts, and equipment/supply procurement. Help maintain and update social media presence for SB&T and/or collaborate with student interns. Uphold ethical standards and maintain confidentiality regarding student records, faculty discussions, and other sensitive information. Follow all college policies. Facilitate the creation of a GA Training Manual for the School of Business and Technology. Provide advising support (as needed). Be an ambassador for the School of Business and Technology and Missouri Valley College. Other duties as assigned. Relevant Professional Skills Developed (related to Graduate Degree Program): Understand the processes and procedures of an academic institution and its departments Collaboration with college employees, administrators, and students/Interpersonal Skills Verbal and written communication skills Problem-solving, critical thinking, analytical skills Time management skills Understand the standards of a professional work environment Understand institutional policies and standards of ethical conduct Google Workspace Applications Microsoft Office Applications Ellucian/Colleague use and navigation Canvas use and navigation To apply, please email a letter of interest and resume to Milena Simic at simicm@moval.edu Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. May require occasional overnight travel. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Graduate Assistant - Baseball The Athletic Department at Missouri Valley College invites applications for a full-time graduate assistant for the baseball program. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Assist in the daily functions of running a successful varsity and varsity reserve baseball program. This will include coaching, recruiting, travel arrangements,  individual skill development, office administration work, and other responsibilities to be discussed. Qualifications Completion of a Bachelor’s degree before the start of the assistantship, acceptance into an applied graduate program, have a minimum of a 2.5 undergraduate GPA, or 3.0 if any graduate work has been completed prior to being hired and all international students wishing to work must have a Social Security number. Playing or coaching experience Communication skill Internet savvy and able to conduct targeted searches Social Media experience Ability to navigate recruiting databases Application Instructions To apply, please email a letter of interest and resume to Coach Mike DeMilia at demiliam@moval.edu . Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. May require occasional overnight travel. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Graduate Assistant for Greek Life The Office of Student Affairs at Missouri Valley College invites applications for a full-time graduate assistant for Greek Life. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Social Media Management: Assist in developing and executing a comprehensive social media strategy for Missouri Valley College Greek Life, including content creation, scheduling, and engagement across various platforms (e.g., Instagram, Facebook, TikTok). Data Tracking and Reporting: Maintain accurate records and data related to Greek organizations, including membership numbers, academic performance, philanthropic efforts, and community service hours. Generate regular reports to assess organizational health and identify areas for improvement. Expansion & Extension Efforts: Support the Greek Life Coordinator in efforts to explore and implement expansion and extension opportunities for new or returning fraternity and sorority chapters on campus, including research, outreach, and logistical support. Recruitment and Membership Development: Assist with the planning, promotion, and execution of formal and informal recruitment events for all Greek-letter organizations. Develop and implement strategies to increase student interest and participation in Greek Life. Meeting Attendance & Support: Attend regular meetings with the Greek Life Coordinator, student leaders, and relevant campus committees (e.g., Greek Council, Order of Omega). Prepare meeting agendas, take minutes, and follow up on action items as directed. Risk Management & Compliance: Ensure all Greek organizations complete mandatory risk management training sessions. Assist in the development and dissemination of risk management resources and policies to promote a safe and responsible Greek community. Program and Event Support: Assist with the planning, promotion, and execution of Greek Life events and initiatives, including leadership development programs, educational workshops, recognition ceremonies, and philanthropic events. Advisory Support: Provide guidance and support to individual chapters and Greek Council as needed, fostering positive interfraternal/intersororal relations and promoting adherence to college policies and national organization guidelines. Resource Development: Assist in the creation and updating of resources for Greek-letter organizations, including handbooks, training materials, and promotional flyers. Administrative Support: Perform general administrative duties as assigned, including maintaining files, responding to inquiries, and assisting with correspondence. On-Call Responsibilities: May require occasional evening and weekend hours to support Greek Life events and activities . Qualifications Completion of a Bachelor’s degree before the start of the assistantship, acceptance into an applied graduate program, have a minimum of a 2.5 undergraduate GPA, or 3.0 if any graduate work has been completed prior to being hired and all international students wishing to work must have a Social Security number. Proficient in written and verbal communication Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously Prior experience in Greek Life (e.g., collegiate member, chapter officer) is preferred but not required Innovative and having the ability to adapt to ever changing situations Application Instructions To apply, please email a letter of interest and resume to Austin Kostelnik (Greek Life Coordinator) at agk9961@moval.edu Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. May require occasional overnight travel. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Graduate Assistant – Institutional Advancement and Alumni Relations Position Summary: The Graduate Assistant (GA) for Institutional Advancement and Alumni Relations at Missouri Valley College will support efforts to engage alumni, donors, and friends of the College through communications, events, and data management. This position offers valuable professional development in the areas of nonprofit management, alumni engagement, fundraising, and event coordination. The GA will work closely with staff to help execute key programs that support the mission and strategic goals of the Office of Institutional Advancement. Key Responsibilities: Assist in the planning and execution of alumni events, including Homecoming, reunions, and regional gatherings. Coordinate communication efforts such as email campaigns, alumni newsletters, and social media posts. Help maintain and update the alumni and donor database with accurate and timely information. Research and write alumni updates and class notes for newsletters and publications. Support preparation and logistics for fundraising initiatives, including giving days and donor stewardship. Provide administrative support such as mailings, RSVP tracking, and event supply organization. Assist with on-campus and off-campus events, including setup, staffing, and follow-up. Collaborate with other departments (athletics, student life, academics) to enhance alumni and campus community connections. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Alumni and Community Engagement. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and acceptance into a Missouri Valley College graduate program. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office; familiarity with Canva or design software is a plus. Social media and digital communication experience preferred. Self-motivated with the ability to work independently and in a team setting. Evening and weekend availability may be required for select events. Work Hours: Approximately 15–20 hours per week during the academic year. Some evening and weekend hours required for event support. Professional Development Opportunities: Gain experience in nonprofit and higher education advancement operations. Learn about alumni engagement strategies, fundraising campaigns, and event coordination. Build a network within the MVC alumni and donor community. Application Instructions To apply, please email a letter of interest and resume to Regan Godsey  at RNG8002@moval.edu. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. May require occasional overnight travel. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Graduate Assistant - Production Assistant KMVC and the Viking Sports Network at Missouri Valley College invites applications for a full-time graduate assistant for a Production Assistant. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Setup and execute Missouri Valley’s Viking Sports Network broadcasts, including a combination of, or all, of the following: setting up audio and video equipment, running and securing cables, verifying operations, operations, taking down equipment before, during and after broadcasts. Qualifications Completion of a Bachelor’s degree before the start of the assistantship, acceptance into an applied graduate program. All international students wishing to work must have a Social Security number Degrees involving mass communication, especially broadcast, preferred Knowledge of Missouri Valley sports, the Heart of America Athletic conference teams, the NAIA and the rules of the sports for broadcast preferred, with the understanding that mastery is an eventual requirement Excellent oral communication skills required Technologically minded, preferred. Must be able to lift 50 lbs. Must be able to work nights, weekends and holidays Application Instructions To apply, please email a letter of interest and resume to Chaz Maddi . Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. May require occasional overnight travel. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Adjunct Instructor, Nursing and Health Sciences Missouri Valley College invites applications for Adjunct Instructor positions across multiple disciplines in the School of Nursing and Health Sciences. We seek dedicated educators committed to excellence in teaching, student success, and the college’s mission. Both on-campus and online teaching opportunities are available. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Teach assigned course(s) as scheduled and outlined in the contract. Foster student success through engaging instruction and intellectual inquiry. Develop and distribute a comprehensive syllabus aligned with institutional guidelines. Implement initiatives to enhance student learning outcomes. Provide timely feedback and support to students. Maintain a respectful, inclusive, and productive learning environment. Collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues and administrators. Complete assigned administrative tasks with accuracy and adherence to deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, procedures, and requirements. Responsibilities listed are representative but not exhaustive of the position. Qualifications : Undergraduate program positions require a Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the relevant discipline from an accredited institution. Graduate program positions require a terminal degree in the discipline. A Terminal Degree (PhD, EdD, etc.) in the relevant discipline is preferred. Previous college or university teaching experience is preferred. Equivalent education, training, and experience may be considered. Physical Demands : Ability to teach and engage with students for extended periods. Capability to stand or sit for prolonged durations. Regular attendance is essential. Reasonable accommodations may be made for individuals with disabilities. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities : Strong ability to interact effectively with students, faculty, and diverse communities. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication, organizational, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently and effectively in an online or in-person setting. Commitment to professionalism and student-centered instruction. Familiarity with Google Workspace (preferred). Experience with Learning Management Systems (required). Online instructors must complete the MVC Online Masterclass. Work Environment : Online Instructors: Home office setting. On-Campus Instructors: Classroom and office settings. Required Technology (Online Instructors Only): Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Reliable high-speed Internet connection (Chrome browser required). Additional Information: Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment is contingent upon a successful background check. Compensation varies by course, enrollment, and program type. Application Instructions: Please send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to: Office of Academic Affairs Dr. Joe Alsobrook alsobrookj@moval.edu References will not be contacted without prior approval from candidates. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment. We do not discriminate based on race, color, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and institutional needs. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society. Adjunct Instructor, Business and Technology Missouri Valley College’s School of Business & Technology invites applications for Adjunct Instructor positions across multiple disciplines. We seek dedicated educators committed to excellence in teaching, student success, and the college’s mission. Both on-campus and online teaching opportunities are available. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Teach assigned course(s) as scheduled and outlined in the contract. Foster student success through engaging instruction and intellectual inquiry. Develop and distribute a comprehensive syllabus aligned with institutional guidelines. Implement initiatives to enhance student learning outcomes. Provide timely feedback and support to students. Maintain a respectful, inclusive, and productive learning environment. Collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues and administrators. Complete assigned administrative tasks with accuracy and adherence to deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, procedures, and requirements. Responsibilities listed are representative but not exhaustive of the position. Qualifications: A Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the relevant discipline from an accredited institution is required. A Terminal Degree (Ph.D., DBA, Ed.D., etc.) in the relevant discipline is preferred. Previous college or university teaching experience is preferred. Equivalent education, training, and experience may be considered. Physical Demands: Ability to teach and engage with students for extended periods. Capability to stand or sit for prolonged durations. Regular attendance is essential. Reasonable accommodations may be made for individuals with disabilities. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong ability to interact effectively with students, faculty, and diverse communities. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication, organizational, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently and effectively in an online or in-person setting. Commitment to professionalism and student-centered instruction. Familiarity with Google Workspace (preferred). Experience with Brightspace or similar Learning Management Systems (required). Online instructors must complete the MVC Online Masterclass. Work Environment: Online Instructors: Home office setting. On-Campus Instructors: Classroom and office settings. Required Technology (Online Instructors Only): Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Reliable high-speed Internet connection (Chrome browser required). Additional Information: Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment is contingent upon a successful background check. Compensation varies by course, enrollment, and program type. Application Instructions: Please send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to: Office of Academic Affairs Dean Milena Simic simicm@moval.edu References will not be contacted without prior approval from candidates. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment. We do not discriminate based on race, color, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and institutional needs. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society. Adjunct Instructor Science & Agriculture Missouri Valley College invites applications for Adjunct Instructor positions across multiple disciplines in the School of Science and Agriculture. We seek dedicated educators committed to excellence in teaching, student success, and the college’s mission. Both on-campus and online teaching opportunities are available. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Teach assigned course(s) as scheduled and outlined in the contract. Foster student success through engaging instruction and intellectual inquiry. Develop and distribute a comprehensive syllabus aligned with institutional guidelines. Conduct regular laboratory sessions in accordance with student learning outcomes. Implement initiatives to enhance student learning outcomes. Provide timely feedback and support to students. Maintain a respectful, inclusive, and productive learning environment. Collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues and administrators. Complete assigned administrative tasks with accuracy and adherence to deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, procedures, and requirements. Responsibilities listed are representative but not exhaustive of the position. Qualifications: A Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the relevant discipline from an accredited institution is required. A Terminal Degree (Ph.D., Ed.D., etc.) in the relevant discipline is preferred. Previous college or university teaching experience is preferred. Equivalent education, training, and experience may be considered. Physical Demands: Ability to teach and engage with students for extended periods. Capability to stand or sit for prolonged durations. Regular attendance is essential. Reasonable accommodations may be made for individuals with disabilities. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong ability to interact effectively with students, faculty, and diverse communities. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication, organizational, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently and effectively in an online or in-person setting. Commitment to professionalism and student-centered instruction. Familiarity with Google Workspace (preferred). Experience with Brightspace or similar Learning Management Systems (required). Online instructors must complete the MVC Online Masterclass. Work Environment: Online Instructors: Home office setting. On-Campus Instructors: Classroom, laboratory, and office settings. Required Technology (Online Instructors Only): Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Reliable high-speed Internet connection (Chrome browser required). Additional Information: Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment is contingent upon a successful background check. Compensation varies by course, enrollment, and program type. Application Instructions: Please send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to: Office of Academic Affairs Dean Andrew Linsenbardt linsenbardta@moval.edu References will not be contacted without prior approval from candidates. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment. We do not discriminate based on race, color, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and institutional needs. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society. Adjunct Instructor - Arts and Humanities Missouri Valley College invites applications for adjunct Instructor positions across the School of Arts and Humanities. We seek dedicated educators committed to excellence in teaching, student success, and the college’s mission. Both on-campus and online teaching opportunities are available. Essential Job Functions & Responsibilities: Teach assigned course(s) as scheduled and outlined in the contract. Foster student success through engaging instruction and intellectual inquiry. Develop and distribute a comprehensive syllabus aligned with institutional guidelines. Implement initiatives to enhance student learning outcomes. Provide timely feedback and support to students. Maintain a respectful, inclusive, and productive learning environment. Collaborate and communicate effectively with colleagues and administrators. Complete assigned administrative tasks with accuracy and adherence to deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, procedures, and requirements. Responsibilities listed are representative but not exhaustive of the position. Qualifications: A Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in the relevant discipline from an accredited institution is required. A Terminal Degree (Ph.D., Ed.D., etc.) in the relevant discipline is preferred. Previous college or university teaching experience is preferred. Equivalent education, training, and experience may be considered. Physical Demands: Ability to teach and engage with students for extended periods. Capability to stand or sit for prolonged durations. Regular attendance is essential. Reasonable accommodations may be made for individuals with disabilities. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong ability to interact effectively with students, faculty, and diverse communities. Critical thinking and problem-solving skills. Excellent communication, organizational, and time-management skills. Ability to work independently and effectively in an online or in-person setting. Commitment to professionalism and student-centered instruction. Familiarity with Google Workspace (preferred). Experience with Brightspace or similar Learning Management Systems (required). Online instructors must complete the MVC Online Masterclass. Work Environment: Online Instructors: Home office setting. On-Campus Instructors: Classroom and office settings. Required Technology (Online Instructors Only): Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Reliable high-speed Internet connection (Chrome browser required). Additional Information : Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment is contingent upon a successful background check. Compensation varies by course, enrollment, and program type. Application Instructions: Please send a cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to Dean Kelley McKay Fuemmeler at mckayk@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior approval from candidates. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment. We do not discriminate based on race, color, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and institutional needs. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts institution located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its diverse and student-focused environment, MVC provides an engaging educational experience that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong learning. Through innovative teaching and interdisciplinary learning, MVC empowers students to succeed in a knowledge-driven global society. Academic Services Graduate Assistant Job Title: Academic Services Graduate Assistant Location: Marshall, Missouri Reports To : Samantha Perkins Open Date: January 6, 2025 Closing Date: Open until filled Murrell Library & Academic Support Center at Missouri Valley College invites applications for a full-time graduate assistant for an Academic Services Graduate Assistant. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities The Academic Services Graduate Assistant will play a critical role in managing the Testing Center, supervising Academic Coaches, and ensuring effective communication with Disability Services. This position involves overseeing test proctoring, conducting data analysis, and generating reports to support the Academic Support Services. Responsibilities: Testing Center Management: Oversee the daily operations of the Testing Center, ensuring a smooth and efficient testing environment. Coordinate and schedule test proctoring, including managing test materials and ensuring adherence to testing protocols. Address and resolve any issues that arise during testing sessions. Test Proctoring: Administer and proctor exams for students, ensuring that testing procedures are followed and providing assistance as needed. Maintain the integrity of the testing environment and uphold academic standards. Communication with Disability Services: Act as a liaison between the Testing Center and Disability Services to accommodate students with special testing needs. Implement approved accommodations and modifications for students with disabilities, ensuring compliance with MVC policies. Supervision of Academic Coaches: Supervise and provide support to academic coaches, including training and guiding them in their roles. Monitor and evaluate the performance of academic coaches, providing feedback and addressing any concerns. Data Analysis and Reporting: Collect, analyze, and interpret data related to testing, academic coaching, and other departmental functions. Create and present detailed reports on testing outcomes, student performance, and program effectiveness. Use data to identify trends, areas for improvement, and make recommendations for enhancing academic services. Administrative Support: Assist in the development and maintenance of documentation and procedures related to testing and academic coaching. Perform general administrative tasks as required, including scheduling meetings and managing correspondence. Qualifications Completion of a Bachelor’s degree before the start of the assistantship, acceptance into an applied graduate program, have a minimum of a 2.5 undergraduate GPA, or 3.0 if any graduate work has been completed prior to being hired and all international students wishing to work must have a Social Security number. Effective interpersonal skills; ability to interact productively with students, faculty staff, and other constituents. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Strong organizational skills, the ability to manage multiple tasks, and willingness to work irregular hours. Experience working with diverse student populations, including international students. Basic computer literacy; basic competency in software and database systems (i.e. Microsoft Office, Adobe). Application Instructions To apply, submit a cover letter, detailed resume and contact information for three professional references to: Samantha Perkins, Assistant Dean of Library & Academic Support Services, 500 E. College Street, Marshall, MO 65340 or e-mail perkinss@moval.edu . Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and committed to a diverse and inclusive environment. Missouri Valley College does not discriminate on the grounds of color, race, sex, religion, marital status, disability, national origin, veteran’s status, age, or sexual orientation. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. All eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. About Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Adjunct Instructor of English The School of Arts and Humanities invites applications for on-campus Adjunct Instructor of English to qualified individuals. Collegiality, professionalism, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence and the college mission are required. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Teach assigned course(s) as specified in the course schedule and contract. Guide students to succeed through personal instruction and intellectual inquiry. Prepare and distribute to students a complete and comprehensive syllabus as per institutional guidelines for every course taught. Undertake and monitor initiatives to improve student learning. Respond to student work, communications, and requests in a timely manner. Maintain a positive, productive, and respectful classroom environment. Communicate, collaborate, and coordinate work with colleagues in a timely manner. Complete assigned or accepted responsibilities, including routine administrative tasks, with accuracy and attention to detail by established deadlines. Comply with all institutional policies, requirements, and procedures. Representative, but not all inclusive, of the essential job functions/responsibilities required for this position. Qualifications Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in English from an accredited institution required. Terminal degree in English or a related field from an accredited institution preferred. Previous teaching experience in a college or university setting preferred. In evaluating candidates for this position, a combination of education, training, and experience which provides the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position may be considered. Physical Demands Stamina to teach classes as required. Ability to stand or sit for extended time periods. Regular attendance is a necessary and essential function. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to engage in effective interactions with students, employees, alumni, and other stakeholders, including individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Ability to think critically and solve problems independently. Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills. Ability to work effectively and independently in a remote teaching environment with minimal supervision. Ability to provide an unwavering example of professionalism. Working knowledge of Google Workspace preferred. Working knowledge of Brightspace or an equivalent learning management system required. Ability to successfully complete the MVC Online Masterclass (applies to online instructors only). Representative, but not all-inclusive, of the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for this position. Work Environment Home Office (Online Instructors) General classroom and office settings (On-campus Instructors) Required Technology (Online Instructors Only) Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Dependable, high-speed Internet access. The required browser is Chrome. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Compensation varies by course based on student enrollment and program type. Application Instructions Please send cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to Kelley McKay Fuemmeler at mckayk@moval.edu . References will not be contacted without prior knowledge and approval of candidates. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Adjunct Instructor of Agriculture Position Type : Adjunct Instructor Location : Online FSLA : Exempt Schoo l: Science & Agriculture Program : Agricultural Systems Management Reports To : Dean Open Date : February 16, 2024 Closing Date : Open until filled Job Summary The School of Science & Agriculture at Missouri Valley College invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor of Agriculture to qualified individuals. Collegiality, professionalism, and a strong commitment to teaching excellence and the college mission are required. Essential Job Functions/Responsibilities Teach assigned course(s) as specified in the course schedule and contract. Guide students to succeed through personal instruction* and intellectual inquiry.* Guide students to become independent learners. Prepare and distribute to students a complete and comprehensive syllabus as per institutional guidelines for every course taught. Administer either an exam or other evaluative activity during the official final exam schedule for every course taught. Determine final grades as per the method prescribed in the syllabus. Provide students with written notice of substantial change(s) to the syllabus. Require use of the course text(s) to an extent that warrants purchase. Undertake and monitor initiatives to improve student learning. Respond to student work, communications, and requests in a timely manner. Submit attendance reports and retention alerts as required or requested. Support safe, orderly, and ethical work and classroom environments. Communicate, collaborate, and coordinate work with colleagues in a timely manner. Complete assigned or accepted responsibilities, including routine administrative tasks, with accuracy and attention to detail by established deadlines. Support the planning, preparation, and submission of assessment and accreditation reports. Comply with all institutional policies, requirements, and procedures. Perform additional duties as requested by the dean. Qualifications Master’s Degree with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in an Agriculture-related subject (e.g., Agronomy, Soil Science, Forestry, Agricultural Education, etc.) from an accredited institution required. Terminal degree in Agriculture or a related field from an accredited institution preferred. Previous teaching experience required; online teaching experience in a college or university setting preferred. In evaluating candidates for this position, a combination of education, training, and experience which provides the necessary knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the essential duties and responsibilities of the position may be considered. Physical Demands Stamina to teach classes as required. Ability to stand or sit for extended time periods. Regular attendance is a necessary and essential function. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse communities and cultures. Ability to think critically and solve problems independently. Excellent communication, organizational, and time management skills. Ability to work effectively and independently in a remote teaching environment with minimal supervision. Ability to provide an unwavering example of professionalism. Working knowledge of Google Workspace preferred. Working knowledge of Brightspace or an equivalent learning management system required. Ability to successfully complete the Missouri Valley College Online Instructor Orientation Course. Representative, but not all-inclusive, of the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for this position. Work Environment Home Office Required Technology Desktop or laptop computer with webcam and microphone. Dependable, high-speed Internet access. The recommended browser is Chrome. Additional Information As a pre-condition of employment, the applicant must be authorized to work in the United States. Employment at MVC is contingent upon satisfactory completion of background check. Compensation varies by course based on student enrollment and program type. Application Instructions Please send cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references to Andrew Linsenbardt, Dean of the School of Science & Agriculture, at linsenbardta@moval.edu . Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Missouri Valley College Founded in 1889, Missouri Valley College is a private, four-year liberal arts college located in Marshall, Missouri. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, Missouri Valley College offers many opportunities to grow in mind, body, and spirit. Faculty are personally and professionally engaged in preparing thoughtful citizens for meaningful lives and careers. Grounded in the liberal arts, undergraduate and graduate studies empower students to master interdisciplinary skills needed to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Stewardship of resources will sustain innovative teaching to stimulate critical thinking, creativity, aesthetic appreciation, and the joys of lifelong learning. Graduate Assistant for Student Affairs Missouri Valley College a private, coeducational, career-oriented, liberal arts college with growing national and international outreach, a destination for students from all fifty states and forty foreign countries. Known for its dynamic, richly diverse, and friendly educational environment, the College prepares students to succeed in a knowledge-based global society. Missouri Valley College  has a student body of some 1,400, on a beautiful campus in west central Missouri. Position Summary: The Graduate Assistant (GA) is responsible for providing student-centered support for the various Student Affairs departments and services. This position provides professional apprenticeship for the GA while supporting essential programs and services for the College community.  Duties will vary based on specific assignments. Assignments may be changed at any time during employment based on the needs of the division. The GA must be accepted into an accredited graduate program for the duration of their contract. Priority will be given to students enrolled in one of the two Missouri Valley College master’s programs. Responsibilities: Serve as building supervisor for the Malcolm Center for Student Life; open and close the building, setup meeting spaces, provide basic housekeeping services. Aid guests in reserving Student Center space and equipment. Assist in the development and implementation of campus activity programming. Assist in the development and implementation of intramural sports programming. Supervise numerous Student Center assistants (work-study). Staff Office of Student Affairs; provide basic administrative support for staff and customer service for guests. Assist in the operation of the Viking Shuttle. All other duties as assigned. Qualifications: Earned bachelor’s degree in any discipline. (In some cases candidates who are in their final year of an undergraduate degree my apply). Effective interpersonal skills; ability to interact productively with students, faculty staff, and other constituents. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Strong organizational skills, the ability to manage multiple tasks, and wiliness to work irregular hours. Experience working with diverse student populations, including international students. Basic computer literacy; basic competency in software and database systems (i.e. Microsoft Office, Adobe). Experience in various forms of advertising, including social media. Compensation: Tuition scholarship, campus housing, and meal plan (when school is in session). Application: To apply, submit a letter of application (cover letter), detailed resume and contact information for three professional references to: Dr. Terry Russell, Vice President for Student Affair, 500 E. College Street, Marshall, MO 65340 or e-mail russellt@moval.edu . This position will remain open until filled. Equal Opportunity Employer Missouri Valley College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and adheres to the Civil Rights Act of 1964, as amended, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, and other legislation prohibiting discrimination in employment and access to educational programs. Employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs. We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive environment, and all eligible candidates are encouraged to apply. Sidebar Request Information Apply to MVC Visit Missouri Valley University 500 East College Street Marshall, Missouri 65340 660-831-4000 © 2026 Missouri Valley University Plan a Visit Faculty & Staff Directory Careers & Opportunities Report a Concern/Crime/Incident Viking Shuttle & Transportation Campus Store Accreditation ADA Annual Clery Report Student Consumer Information Student Catalog and Handbook Privacy Policy Follow Us Missouri Valley on Twitter Missouri Valley on Facebook Missouri Valley on YouTube Missouri Valley on Instagram"
